IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation: Part 3 Division 2, ss 23 and 24.
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively). The company's capacity and powers (s 23) and its power to provide for employees on a cessation of business (s 24).
-- s 23(2) to (5) are shown "[Deleted by Act 17 of 2023 wef 01/07/2023]" in the text and are not encoded (NOTES.md, coverage table).
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer; NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (sgi)").
--   JUST TRUE  = the section's own test is met on the facts given.
--   JUST FALSE = the text says no to this case in its own words (comment `FALSE-kind`).
--   NOTHING    = the text does not say (comment `NOTHING-kind`). A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- The text is a rendering of the Act (an informal consolidation turned from PDF into plain text), not the official text.

§ `Section 23(1): the company's full capacity, rights, powers and privileges`

-- "Subject to the provisions of this Act and any other written law and its constitution, a company has full capacity ..."
-- is a liberty with three exceptions. The three exceptions are plain inputs: whether a provision of this Act, of another written law
-- or of the constitution limits the capacity for the act asked about. The sources do not say which provisions do (they are elsewhere
-- in this Act, in other Acts, and in the company's own constitution), so the encoding cannot say it for the person.
-- src:4179 | 23.—(1) Subject to the provisions of this Act and any other written
-- src:4180 | law and its constitution, a company has —
-- src:4182 | (a) full capacity to carry on or undertake any business or
-- src:4183 | activity, do any act or enter into any transaction; and
@ref s 23(1)(a) (src:4179-4183)
GIVEN `a provision of this Act limits the company's capacity to do the act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another written law limits the company's capacity to do the act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company's constitution limits the company's capacity to do the act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 23(1)(a) the company has full capacity to carry on or undertake the business or activity, do the act or enter into the transaction` MEANS
    IF    (NOT `a provision of this Act limits the company's capacity to do the act`)
      AND (NOT `another written law limits the company's capacity to do the act`)
      AND (NOT `the company's constitution limits the company's capacity to do the act`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to the provisions of this Act and any other written law and its constitution, a company has full capacity ..." -- a grant limited by its own wording; where a limit applies the text names no outcome (fork line F-I1 in NOTES.md)

-- src:4179 | 23.—(1) Subject to the provisions of this Act and any other written
-- src:4180 | law and its constitution, a company has —
-- src:4182 | (a) full capacity to carry on or undertake any business or
-- src:4183 | activity, do any act or enter into any transaction; and
-- src:4188 | (b) for the purposes of paragraph (a), full rights, powers and
-- src:4189 | privileges.
@ref s 23(1)(b) (src:4179-4189)
GIVEN `the rights, powers and privileges are for the purposes of the business, activity, act or transaction in paragraph (a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a provision of this Act limits the company's capacity to do the act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another written law limits the company's capacity to do the act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company's constitution limits the company's capacity to do the act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 23(1)(b) the company has full rights, powers and privileges for the purposes of paragraph (a)` MEANS
    IF    `the rights, powers and privileges are for the purposes of the business, activity, act or transaction in paragraph (a)`
      AND (NOT `a provision of this Act limits the company's capacity to do the act`)
      AND (NOT `another written law limits the company's capacity to do the act`)
      AND (NOT `the company's constitution limits the company's capacity to do the act`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for the purposes of paragraph (a), full rights, powers and privileges" under the same "Subject to ..." -- a grant whose limit is met or whose purpose is not paragraph (a)'s; the text names no outcome (F-I1)

§ `Sections 23(1A) and 23(1B): objects, and restrictions, in the constitution`

-- src:4193 | (1A) A company may have the objects of the company included in
-- src:4194 | its constitution.
@ref s 23(1A) (src:4193-4194)
GIVEN `the provision states the objects of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 23(1A) the company may have its objects included in its constitution` MEANS
    IF `the provision states the objects of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "A company may have the objects of the company included in its constitution." says nothing of a provision that is not the objects of the company

-- src:4198 | (1B) The constitution of a company may contain a provision
-- src:4199 | restricting its capacity, rights, powers or privileges.
@ref s 23(1B) (src:4198-4199)
GIVEN `the provision restricts the company's capacity, rights, powers or privileges` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 23(1B) the constitution may contain the provision` MEANS
    IF `the provision restricts the company's capacity, rights, powers or privileges`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "The constitution of a company may contain a provision restricting its capacity, rights, powers or privileges." says nothing of any other kind of provision (s 23(1B) is a permission and not a closed list)

§ `Section 24: provision for employees on a cessation of business`

-- src:4214 | 24.—(1) The powers of a company are, if they would not otherwise
-- src:4215 | do so, deemed to include power to make provision, in connection with
-- src:4216 | any cessation of the whole or any part of the business carried on by
-- src:4217 | the company or any subsidiary of the company, for the benefit of
-- src:4218 | persons employed or formerly employed by the company or its
-- src:4219 | subsidiary.
@ref s 24(1) (src:4214-4219)
GIVEN `the provision is made in connection with a cessation of the whole or any part of the business carried on by the company or any subsidiary of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision is for the benefit of persons employed or formerly employed by the company or its subsidiary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 24(1) the powers of the company are deemed to include power to make the provision` MEANS
    IF    `the provision is made in connection with a cessation of the whole or any part of the business carried on by the company or any subsidiary of the company`
      AND `the provision is for the benefit of persons employed or formerly employed by the company or its subsidiary`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "The powers of a company are, if they would not otherwise do so, deemed to include power ..." -- a deeming that adds a power and says nothing of any other provision (the deeming reaches this provision or it does not)

-- s 24(2): subsection (1) "does not affect any provision in a company's constitution requiring any exercise of the power ... to be approved by the company in general meeting
-- or otherwise prescribing the manner in which that power is to be exercised" -- a flat negative about the effect of subsection (1).
-- src:4221 | (2) Subsection (1) relates only to the capacity of a company as a
-- src:4222 | body corporate and does not affect any provision in a company’s
-- src:4223 | constitution requiring any exercise of the power mentioned in that
-- src:4224 | subsection to be approved by the company in general meeting or
-- src:4225 | otherwise prescribing the manner in which that power is to be
-- src:4226 | exercised.
@ref s 24(2) (src:4221-4226)
GIVEN `the constitution requires the exercise of the power to be approved by the company in general meeting or otherwise prescribes the manner in which the power is to be exercised` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 24(2) subsection (1) affects the constitution's provision on how the power is exercised` MEANS
    IF `the constitution requires the exercise of the power to be approved by the company in general meeting or otherwise prescribes the manner in which the power is to be exercised`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) ... does not affect any provision in a company's constitution requiring any exercise of the power mentioned in that subsection to be approved by the company in general meeting or otherwise prescribing the manner in which that power is to be exercised"
    ELSE NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (silent): where the constitution has no such provision, subsection (2) has nothing to say about what subsection (1) affects
